#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a118fe4a-cd1f-52f7-aa33-59f5494e4905" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Distinct Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c1c3f8-e34c-5913-9027-40cbf9b38b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36c1c3f8-e34c-5913-9027-40cbf9b38b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305677} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6401040-97c5-5632-9c58-3544640ae047" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40844993-f65c-5c72-af9c-ffdf6d82f4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40844993-f65c-5c72-af9c-ffdf6d82f4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305783} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb369d00-0a03-526e-b8a8-28162f18b93d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f28e1404-987d-53df-a0ad-e0b6d8de5b42" :question/math-academy-id "q-334630" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $-1\\pm 2\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}={e}^{-t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 4{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=(-1+2\\text{i})t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=(-1-2\\text{i})t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((-1+2\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(-1+2\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(-1+2\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\ (-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+2{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 2t{\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t+{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2t}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\cdot t+{e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{-t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221409 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a118fe4a-cd1f-52f7-aa33-59f5494e4905" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix Exponent for a Matrix With Distinct Complex Eigenvalues"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cded054f-fd7d-5541-b119-acd319ea1369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cded054f-fd7d-5541-b119-acd319ea1369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307055} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe30a28-0d85-5a80-a24a-88caf298d3fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "173c0281-09d3-5067-b83f-37506d1cb0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "173c0281-09d3-5067-b83f-37506d1cb0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13\\operatorname{sin}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305365} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf013e3-bfec-56fb-abcf-075b57f8eb70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94b786d3-6c88-5e7c-b171-415f525959f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-334637" :question/problem "Find ${e}^{At}$ for $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\pm 5\\text{i}.$*\n\n| ${e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ | $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -13 & -1\\end{bmatrix}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -13{\\alpha }_{1}t & -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are functions to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues or $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5\\text{i}t) & ={e}^{5\\text{i}t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}\\cdot 5\\text{i}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+5{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t &=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-13{\\alpha }_{1}t & =-13\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -13\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & 5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4fc3ba4-d488-5156-88dc-837369269cef" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44269325-ce6a-5455-931e-15b7c67f949e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44269325-ce6a-5455-931e-15b7c67f949e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305820} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f7cd1b4-a3c3-5a92-8505-97219220b6be" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307972} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce17bce7-e09f-50e5-8677-6bf7b0e2a6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce17bce7-e09f-50e5-8677-6bf7b0e2a6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307057} :answer-field/id #uuid "acadd084-eae4-5cdf-a4f3-de1038487b85" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce912870-57f5-5b52-93a9-7294f5ae4c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce912870-57f5-5b52-93a9-7294f5ae4c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307060} :answer-field/id #uuid "d416bd54-772a-557b-b57d-810f93cfad9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d01fa5d3-da0e-5ede-9b2c-b888bb92a4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-2t){e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01fa5d3-da0e-5ede-9b2c-b888bb92a4be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-2t){e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307077} :answer-field/id #uuid "e717c517-fae6-5429-8329-6a601aec689e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf8f7576-f6c0-5d24-9d4e-d8cc050c1036" :question/math-academy-id "q-335093" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} & t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} & t{e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{-2t} & (1-2t){e}^{-2t} \\\\ 0 & -2{e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221411 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4fc3ba4-d488-5156-88dc-837369269cef" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Derivative of a Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c3e688a-d00f-5c7d-bfff-2deb95e138bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{cos}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c3e688a-d00f-5c7d-bfff-2deb95e138bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\operatorname{cos}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306038} :answer-field/id #uuid "10f8227c-1448-5bfe-9e64-cdcfa325f853" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c408733a-e25b-5774-baf1-164003c5f78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{cos}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c408733a-e25b-5774-baf1-164003c5f78a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{cos}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306977} :answer-field/id #uuid "15ce0198-a457-52fa-a17d-46133d696ab4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ec9fbd1-bfcf-5774-b8c2-55e9dfa32371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{sin}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ec9fbd1-bfcf-5774-b8c2-55e9dfa32371" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{sin}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306368} :answer-field/id #uuid "e30e1dd1-cc02-52f7-af40-22cd31c5cfdd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d151806-374d-547d-a63e-b2a3f75a7fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{sin}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d151806-374d-547d-a63e-b2a3f75a7fe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10\\operatorname{sin}(10t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306487} :answer-field/id #uuid "e87e6353-67e7-5e70-80d8-7d8a533a69bf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec4ec1fa-f063-5a3c-ba78-66239dbbdec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335096" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nGiven the matrices $A$ and ${e}^{At}$ above, compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}).$\n\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At})=A\\,{e}^{At}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{At}) & =A\\,{e}^{At} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -10 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t) & -10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) \\\\ 10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10t) & -10\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
